1	//! Offline `pets_tiny.bin` builder. Saga 29 step 003.
2	//!
3	//! Reads the gitignored Oxford-IIIT Pet image checkout from
4	//! `data/oxford-iiit-pet/images/`, picks 100 cat + 100 dog
5	//! images, decodes + resizes each to 64x64 u8 RGB, and writes
6	//! `crates/mlpl-eval/data/pets_tiny.bin` in the wire format
7	//! that `src/pets_tiny.rs` expects.
8	//!
9	//! Convention: Oxford-IIIT Pet filenames distinguish cat
10	//! vs dog by case -- capitalized = cat breed
11	//! (`Abyssinian_1.jpg`), lowercase = dog breed
12	//! (`beagle_3.jpg`). The label byte is `0` for cat and `1`
13	//! for dog so a binary classifier targets `Y` directly.
14	//!
15	//! Build + run with the `image-io` feature enabled:
16	//!
17	//! ```bash
18	//! cargo run --example build_pets_tiny \
19	//!   --features image-io -p mlpl-eval
20	//! ```
21	//!
22	//! The committed `pets_tiny.bin` lands at
23	//! `crates/mlpl-eval/data/pets_tiny.bin` and is shipped via
24	//! `include_bytes!` -- after running this, `git add` and
25	//! commit the new fixture in the same step that wires
26	//! `load_preloaded("pets_tiny")` end-to-end.
